  "id": "BIT-postgresql-2026-14671",
  "summary": "PostgreSQL refint plan cache type confusion executes arbitrary code",
  "details": "Type confusion in PostgreSQL module \"refint\" allows an object creator to execute arbitrary code as the operating system user running the database.  The fix for this emerged as a non-security bug report, and the fix appear in the git repository with subject \"refint: Remove plan cache.\", without a CVE number.  Versions before PostgreSQL 18.6, 17.11, 16.15, 15.19, and 14.24 are affected.",
